### Once upon a time
  -> Once upon a time there was a bear who had a problem. He was confused when he realised he couldn't find his way home. He looked around and saw a little girl in the forest with a light. The bear ran up to her and said, "Hi, I'm Bob. What are you looking for?" / The girl replied, "I'm trying to find my way home. Can you help me, I'm suffering?" / Bob smiled and said, "Of course I can. I'm here to help you." / The bear and the girl walked through the forest together until they found the girl's home. She was so happy! / Bob felt good that he had been able to help the girl. / The girl smiled and said, "Let's go home now. We will never forget you!" / And so Bob and the girl were the best of friends.
  -> Once upon a time, in a small town, there was a little girl named Lucy. Lucy loved to play with her soft toy cat, named Teddy. Teddy was her best friend. They played every day and had lots of fun together. / One sunny Tuesday, Lucy and Teddy went to a store. Lucy asked her mom if they could buy Teddy. Her mom said, "Yes, we can buy Teddy today." Lucy and Teddy were so happy. / At the store, Lucy saw a big, red ball. She asked her mom, "Can I buy the ball, please?" Her mom said, "Yes, but you must carry it home." Lucy smiled and held the ball tight. / Lucy and her mom bought the ball and went home. They played with the ball all day. When it was time to go home, Lucy gave Teddy a big hug and said, "I love you, Teddy!" Teddy hugged her back, and they went to bed, tired but happy from their day together.
  -> Once upon a time, there was a little boy named Tim. Tim had a toy motorcycle that he loved very much. Every day, he would play with his motorcycle and make it go fast. One day, Tim's mom told him about a big race for kids. Tim was very excited and wanted to win the race. / The next day, Tim woke up early and ran to the park. He saw the big motorcycle there. It was the fastest motorcycle! Tim wanted to race it too. He knew his mom would always be dependable, just like him. So, Tim ran to his motorcycle and started to race his toy motorcycle. / As Tim ran, the motorcycle went faster and faster. He was so close that he could almost reach the finish line. Tim was a little bit scared, but he kept going. In the end, Tim crossed the finish line and won the race! Tim was so happy and felt so proud. His mom was proud of him.

